From 73394d31f6cdef404acb5b5d49baa7f19eaad74b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:26:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): avoid empty historical think blocks and doubled
 tool separators
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completed assistant messages without reasoning_content under tools previously
opened <think> on the preceding turn and immediately closed </think>, producing
out-of-distribution <｜Assistant｜><think></think> pairs across multi-turn tool
histories, while streamed assistant.content ending in \n\n doubled to \n\n\n\n
before <｜DSML｜ calls> on replay and None-valued reasoning fields overwrote
populated reasoning_content during message normalization.

Render completed assistant turns lacking reasoning_content as <｜Assistant｜></think>
(matching dropped-thinking history turns while preserving non-empty
reasoning_content and wo_eos prefix continuations), trim one trailing \n\n from
assistant content before appending \n\n<｜DSML｜ calls>, and preserve
reasoning_content when an explicit None reasoning key is present.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Prevents multi-turn <think></think> imitation (0-token reasoning skips), \n\n\n\n separator drift, and clobbered reasoning_content in OpenAI-compatible multi-turn tool loops.
Quality: Prompt-encoding fix for completed historical assistant turns without reasoning_content and streamed pre-tool content ending in \n\n; all official DeepSeek V4.1 reference fixtures, non-empty reasoning_content turns, and prefix=True continuations are byte-identical.
Tests: pytest tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41_effort.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41_renderer_pool.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v4.py (188 passed).
Upstream-status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 prompt encoding fix.
